	// Ordered, and the order is the client's to set - new pins go on the end, so a dial does not reshuffle under a thumb. Entries are station PIDs (`rs-...`) and are not resolved on write: a station deleted by another household member leaves its pid here, and a client renders only the pids it can still find, because failing a whole preference write over one departed station would be worse than a dial one slot shorter.
